#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#A VS solver program can be loaded and run from a Python file. This example is described in a tech memo accessed from Help > Technical Memos > Example: Automating Runs with the VS API.
#
#If you want to use the feature which allows you to save multiple sets of results, the ring control must be set prior generating the files for the run.
#
#To make the run:
#1. Click the button "Generate Files for this Run",
#2. From the folder Extensions\Custom_Py, run the routine VS_Run.py.
#3. Alternatively, run the routine Example_PyVS.py.
#
#For 64-bit Python, please change the linked Model dataset to the 64-bit example.
#
#This example works for Python 3.5.x
#
#Note that this simulation is overlaid with the Quick Start Guide, Baseline example to demonstrate that the simulation results to do not differ between running the Python and the baseline example.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

